No outbound network access at runtime
  Nothing in this distribution contacts a remote service: there is no object-store client,
  no model-hub download and no experiment-tracking upload. Model weights, corpora, tokenizer
  assets and latent indices are all read from local paths, and the repository contains no
  credentials, tokens or endpoint configuration. RynnLAM training metrics are written to a
  local `<output_dir>/<exp_name>/metrics.jsonl`. The one exception is
  `scripts/evaluate_rynnlam.py regress`, which execs a user-supplied external LARYBench
  checkout as a subprocess and forces `WANDB_MODE=disabled` / `WANDB_DISABLED=true` in that
  child's environment.

One listening socket: the VLABench policy server
  Files: scripts/vlabench_policy_server.py
  `scripts/vlabench_policy_server.py` opens a TCP server so an external benchmark runner can
  drive a Stage-2 checkpoint. It listens; it does not dial out. The wire format is a 4-byte
  big-endian length, a one-byte message type, then a **pickle** payload, in both directions
  (the full protocol is specified in that file's docstring). Unpickling executes arbitrary
  code, so anyone who can reach the port can run code as the server user. The server therefore
  binds loopback by default and `resolve_bind_host` refuses a reachable address unless
  `--allow-remote-bind` is passed explicitly; keep it that way, and keep the port off any
  network you do not control. The bundled tests pin both the framing and that refusal.
  Nothing else in this distribution listens on a port, and no component sends data anywhere.

Bundled sample data
  Files: data/sample/, data/sample_lam/
  License: this distribution's license (see LICENSE).
  Both are tiny SYNTHETIC corpora generated by scripts/make_sample_data.py and
  scripts/make_sample_lam_data.py: 3 episodes of Stage-1 latent npz / mp4 / index / stats,
  and 3 scenes of preprocessed RynnLAM safetensors. They contain no third-party dataset
  content, no model output and no real robot or video data, and exist only so a fresh clone
  can run `bash scripts/smoke.sh` offline. Every path inside them is repo-root-relative.
  Because the frames and latents are synthetic, the losses they produce are meaningless;
  they prove the pipeline runs, not that a model learns.

No weights or generated fixtures are bundled
  Apart from the synthetic samples above, this distribution contains source code and
  documentation only. No model weights, tokenizer / chat-template / processor assets, real
  datasets, latent corpora, or generated smoke fixtures ship, so no upstream license beyond
  the ones attributed above applies to the contents of this archive. In particular, the
  RynnBrain backbones, the DA3-Large encoder weights that `rynnlam/configs/*.yaml` reference,
  offline RynnLAM latent corpora, the LIBERO datasets and simulator assets, the RoboTwin HDF5
  episodes that `rynnvla/datasets/vla_datasets/robotwin.py` reads, the VLABench simulator tree
  and the benchmark runner that drives `scripts/vlabench_policy_server.py`, and the LARYBench
  archives and regression code that `scripts/evaluate_rynnlam.py` consumes are all obtained
  separately under their own terms. `scripts/make_smoke_tiny_model.py` materializes a tiny
  random-weight backbone under data/smoke_tiny_model/ at runtime; that path is gitignored, so
  no weights ship, but the tokenizer assets it copies from the checkpoint you supply remain
  under their own upstream license. See the "Third-party dependencies and attribution"
  section of README.md.

